@startuml POST /payouts — Submission Flow

skinparam backgroundColor #f5f6f1
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #c7cbb4
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor #ffffff
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor #dbdec9
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam noteBorderColor #c7cbb4
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #f3e8d2

title POST /payouts — Submission & Async Settlement Flow

actor       "Merchant / Caller"   as Caller
participant "API Gateway"         as GW
participant "Payout Service"      as PS
database    "Postgres\n(Ledger)"  as DB
queue       "Kafka"               as Kafka
participant "State Machine\nWorker" as SMW
participant "Partner Rail\n(Bank / Wallet)" as Rail

== 1. Synchronous acceptance (caller waits) ==

Caller -> GW   : POST /payouts\nIdempotency-Key: <uuid>
GW     -> PS   : forward + validate

PS     -> DB   : BEGIN\nSELECT idempotency_key FOR UPDATE\nINSERT payout (status=PENDING)\nCOMMIT
note right of DB : Dedup check + payout creation\nin ONE transaction — no race

DB     --> PS  : payout_id = pyo_xxx

PS     -> Kafka : publish payout.created\n{payout_id, correlation_id}
PS     --> GW  : 202 Accepted
GW     --> Caller : { payout_id, status: PENDING }

note over Caller : Caller persists payout_id\nand polls / awaits webhook

== 2. Async settlement (caller not involved) ==

Kafka  -> SMW  : consume payout.created
SMW    -> DB   : UPDATE status=SUBMITTED\nWHERE status=PENDING   /'single-writer guard'/

SMW    -> Rail : submit payout\nclient_reference = Idempotency-Key
note right of Rail : Reference reused as partner ref —\nenables ambiguous-failure recovery\n(see SUBMITTED_UNCONFIRMED)

alt Happy path
  Rail --> SMW : 200 OK — accepted
  SMW  -> DB   : UPDATE status=SETTLED
  SMW  -> Kafka : publish payout.settled

else Rail rejects (non-retryable)
  Rail --> SMW : 4xx — invalid account / sanctions
  SMW  -> DB   : UPDATE status=FAILED\nfailure_reason=BENEFICIARY_ACCOUNT_INVALID
  SMW  -> Kafka : publish payout.failed

else Connection dropped (outcome unknown)
  Rail --> SMW : timeout / network error
  SMW  -> DB   : UPDATE status=SUBMITTED_UNCONFIRMED
  note right of SMW #f3e8d2 : Do NOT fail over to another rail yet.\nQuery partner using client_reference\nto resolve outcome first.
  SMW  -> Rail : GET /status?ref=<Idempotency-Key>
  Rail --> SMW : resolved outcome
  SMW  -> DB   : UPDATE status=SETTLED | FAILED
end

Kafka -> "Webhook\nDispatcher" as WD : consume payout.settled / failed
WD -> Caller : POST <caller_webhook_url>\nHMAC-signed event

note over Caller : Webhook is a convenience layer —\nGET /payouts/{id} is always\nthe source of truth

@enduml
